  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "An amount of substance per unit volume that is the concentration of a saturated solution expressed as the ratio of the solute concentration over the volume of water.  A substance's solubility fundamentally depends on several physical and chemical properties of the solution as well as the environment it is in.";
