  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "A \"Position Vector\", also known as location vector or radius vector, is a Euclidean vector which represents the position of a point P in space in relation to an arbitrary reference origin O.";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition> "$r = \\overrightarrow{OP}$, where $O$ and $P$ are two points in space."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
