<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Illuminance> a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Beleuchtungsstärke"@de, "Intenzita osvětlení"@cs, "Pencahayaan"@ms, "aydınlanma şiddeti"@tr,
    "illuminamento"@it, "illuminance"@en, "iluminamento"@pt, "iluminare"@ro, "luminosidad"@es,
    "megvilágítás"@hu, "natężenie oświetlenia"@pl, "osvetljenost"@sl, "éclairement lumineux"@fr,
    "Осветеност"@bg, "Освещённость"@ru, "הארה (שטף ליחידת שטח)"@he, "شدة الضوء"@ar, "شدت روشنایی"@fa,
    "प्रदीपन"@hi, "照度"@ja, "照度"@zh;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:LuminousFluxPerArea";
  dct:description "Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface, per unit area. It is a measure of the intensity of the incident light, wavelength-weighted by the luminosity function to correlate with human brightness perception."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  skos:altLabel "éclairement"@fr;
  skos:broader <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LuminousFluxPerArea>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch> "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Illuminance"^^xsd:anyURI;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-2I1M0H0T0D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code> "0112/2///62720#UAD062";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference> "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illuminance"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec61987/iec61987.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD062"^^xsd:anyURI;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch> <https://si-digital-framework.org/SI/quantities/ILLU>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface, per unit area. It is a measure of the intensity of the incident light, wavelength-weighted by the luminosity function to correlate with human brightness perception.";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition> "$E_v = \\frac{d\\Phi}{dA}$, where $d\\Phi$ is the luminous flux incident on an element of the surface with area $dA$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit> unit:FC, unit:LUX, unit:PHOT .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceProportion> a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:seeAlso <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceRate>;
  rdfs:label "Incidence Proportion"@en;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Incidence";
  dct:description "Incidence proportion (also known as cumulative incidence) is the number of new cases within a specified time period divided by the size of the population initially at risk. For example, if a population initially contains 1,000 non-diseased persons and 28 develop a condition over two years of observation, the incidence proportion is 28 cases per 1,000 persons per two years, i.e. 2.8% per two years."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  skos:broader <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Incidence>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incidence_(epidemiology)"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumulative_incidence"^^xsd:anyURI;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "Incidence proportion (also known as cumulative incidence) is the number of new cases within a specified time period divided by the size of the population initially at risk. For example, if a population initially contains 1,000 non-diseased persons and 28 develop a condition over two years of observation, the incidence proportion is 28 cases per 1,000 persons per two years, i.e. 2.8% per two years.";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit> unit:CASES-PER-KiloINDIV-YR .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceRate> a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:seeAlso <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceProportion>;
  rdfs:label "Incidence Rate"@en;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Incidence";
  dct:description "The incidence rate is a measure of the frequency with which a disease or other incident occurs over a specified time period. It is also known as the incidence density rate or person-time incidence rate, when the denominator is the combined person-time of the population at risk (the sum of the time duration of exposure across all persons exposed)"^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  skos:broader <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Incidence>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incidence_(epidemiology)"^^xsd:anyURI;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "The incidence rate is a measure of the frequency with which a disease or other incident occurs over a specified time period. It is also known as the incidence density rate or person-time incidence rate, when the denominator is the combined person-time of the population at risk (the sum of the time duration of exposure across all persons exposed)";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit> unit:CASES-PER-KiloINDIV-YR .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MutualInductance> a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:seeAlso <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Inductance>;
  rdfs:label "Mutual Inductance"@en;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Inductance";
  dct:description "$\\textit{Mutual Inductance}$ is the non-diagonal term of the inductance matrix. For two loops, the symbol $M$ is used for $L_{12}$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  skos:broader <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Inductance>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E-2L2I0M1H0T-2D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference> "http://www.iso.org/iso/home/store/catalogue_tc/catalogue_detail.htm?csnumber=31891"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-12-36"^^xsd:anyURI;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol> "L_{mn}";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition> "$L_{mn} = \\frac{\\Psi_m}{I_n}$, where $I_n$ is an electric current in a thin conducting loop $n$ and $\\Psi_m$ is the linked flux caused by that electric current in another loop $m$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit> unit:H, unit:H_Ab, unit:NanoH, unit:H_Stat,
    unit:KiloH, unit:MicroH, unit:MilliH, unit:PicoH .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContent> a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "information content";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code> "0112/2///62720#UAD066";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference> "https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec61987/iec61987.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD066"^^xsd:anyURI .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContentExpressedAsALogarithmToBase10>
  a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "information content expressed as a logarithm to base 10"@en-US;
  dct:description "I(xi) as the information content I(xi) of a result xi (e.g. the occurrence of a character xi) is the common logarithm of the reciprocal of the probability p(xi) of its occurrence, i.e.: l(x) lg 1/p(x) Hart, where p(x) is the probability of the event x"@en;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol> "0173-1#Z4-BAJ468#001";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "(xi) als der Informationsgehalt I(xi) eines Ergebnisses xi (z. B. das Auftreten eines Zeichens xi) ist der dekatischer Logarithmus des Kehrwertes der Wahrscheinlichkeit p (xi) für sein eintreten, also: l(x) lg 1/p(x) Hart, dabei ist p(x) die Wahrscheinlichkeit des Ereignisses x"@de .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContentExpressedAsALogarithmToBase2>
  a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "information content expressed as a logarithm to base 2"@en-US;
  dct:description "I(xi) as the information content I(xi) of a result xi (e.g. the occurrence of a character xi) is the binary logarithm of the reciprocal of the probability p(xi) of its occurrence, i.e.: l(x) lb 1/p(x) Sh, where p(x) is the probability of the event x"@en;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol> "0173-1#Z4-BAJ463#001";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "I(xi) als der Informationsgehalt I(xi) eines Ergebnisses xi (z. B. das Auftreten eines Zeichens xi) ist der binäre Logarithmus des Kehrwertes der Wahrscheinlichkeit p (xi) für sein eintreten, also: l(x) = lb 1/p(x) Sh, dabei ist p(x) die Wahrscheinlichkeit des Ereignisses x"@de .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContentExpressedAsALogarithmToBaseE>
  a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "information content expressed as a logarithm to base e"@en-US;
  dct:description "I(xi) as the information content I(xi) of a result xi (e.g. the occurrence of a character xi) is the natural logarithm of the reciprocal of the probability p(xi) of its occurrence, i.e.: l(x) ln 1/p(x) nat, where p(x) is the probability of the event x"@en;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol> "0173-1#Z4-BAJ469#001";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "I(xi) als der Informationsgehalt I(xi) eines Ergebnisses xi (z. B. das Auftreten eines Zeichens xi) ist der natürliche Logarithmus des Kehrwertes der Wahrscheinlichkeit p (xi) für sein eintreten, also: l(x) = ln 1/p(x) nat, dabei ist p(x) die Wahrscheinlichkeit des Ereignisses x"@de .

