<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Thrust> a <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind>;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Thrust"@en;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Force";
  dct:description """Thrust is a reaction force described quantitatively by Newton's Second and Third Laws. When a system expels or accelerates mass in one direction the accelerated mass will cause a proportional but opposite force on that system.
The pushing or pulling force developed by an aircraft engine or a rocket engine.
The force exerted in any direction by a fluid jet or by a powered screw, as, the thrust of an antitorque rotor.
Specifically, in rocketry, $ F\\,= m\\cdot v$ where m is propellant mass flow and v is exhaust velocity relative to the vehicle. Also called momentum thrust."""^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString>;
  skos:broader <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Force>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch> "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thrust"^^xsd:anyURI;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector> <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-2D0>;
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription> "Thrust is a reaction force described quantitatively by Newton's Second and Third Laws. When a system expels or accelerates mass in one direction the accelerated mass will cause a proportional but opposite force on that system.";
  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit> unit:CentiN, unit:DYN, unit:DeciN, unit:GM_F,
    unit:KIP_F, unit:KiloGM-M-PER-SEC2, unit:N, unit:KiloGM_F, unit:KiloPOND, unit:KiloLB_F,
    unit:KiloN, unit:LB_F, unit:MegaLB_F, unit:MegaN, unit:MicroN, unit:MilliN, unit:OZ_F,
    unit:PDL, unit:POND, unit:PlanckForce, unit:TON_F_US .

